---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_URL } from '../consts';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'About', url: `${SITE_URL}/about/` },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About NSN Explorer: Free Government Parts Data"
  description="NSN Explorer is a free, independent index of U.S. government parts solicitations and prices built from public DIBBS, SAM.gov and USAspending records."
  pageType="AboutPage"
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
  <h1>About {SITE_NAME}</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    NSN Explorer is an independent project built for suppliers who want to find and win federal
    parts work — it indexes public U.S. government procurement records — DIBBS solicitations and
    awards, and USAspending contract data — into one searchable site.
  </p>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <p class="gloss">
    We built it because that data exists but is scattered across systems built for procurement
    officers, not for the businesses that could fill the orders. NSN Explorer renders the same
    public facts clearly: what's open now, per part, over time, with a link back to the source
    record behind every figure — so a supplier can find work and quote it with confidence. The
    same index also serves buyers sizing up a category, researchers and market-watchers tracking
    federal demand, investors watching a sector, and journalists checking a number.
  </p>
  <p class="gloss">
    We are not a government entity and we don't sell parts to the government ourselves on this
    site, and we don't broker or submit bids on anyone's behalf. Every figure here links to the
    public record it came from. Nothing on this site is estimated or modeled — if you find an
    error, tell us and we'll fix it.
  </p>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <p class="gloss">
    Optional accounts sign in through <a href="https://workos.com" rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">WorkOS</a>.
    Watchlists and saved searches are stored with our database provider; see the
    <a href="/privacy/#accounts">privacy policy</a> for what an account keeps.
  </p>

  <p class="gloss" id="crawler">
    <strong>NSNExplorerBot.</strong> For the supplier pages we read a few public pages of each company's own website
    (the home page and, where they exist, its about, capabilities, quality and contact pages) so a supplier's page can say what the
    company says it makes and how to reach it. The crawler identifies itself as
    <code>Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; NSNExplorerBot/1.0; +https://nsnexplorer.com/about/#crawler)</code> (or, if a site refuses that
    once, <code>NSNExplorerBot/1.0 (+https://nsnexplorer.com/about/#crawler)</code>), fetches and obeys the site's
    <code>robots.txt</code>, reads at most four pages per site, waits at least two seconds between requests to one site, and
    revisits a site about twice a year. If you run a website and do not want it read, disallow <code>NSNExplorerBot</code> in
    <code>robots.txt</code> or <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>email us</a>. Suppliers can also ask us to hide their contact
    details or website summary; see <a href="/privacy/#suppliers">Supplier information</a> in the privacy policy.
  </p>

  <p class="gloss">NSN Explorer is operated by NAO Parts LLC.</p>

  <p class="gloss">
    Contact: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
